:name: CAN PoC step 3b: OBC and Experiment on two redundant CAN buses
:description: two_boards.resc plus a second CANHub busB joining both CAN2 controllers. every OBC message goes out on both buses, the experiment board drops the second copy.
:
: how to run (from the top folder, the one with firmware/ and renode/):
:   renode renode/redundant.resc then type: start
:
:   +--- obc ---+               +--- experiment ---+
:   |  can1 ----+---- busA -----+---- can1         |
:   |  can2 ----+---- busB -----+---- can2         |
:   +-----------+               +------------------+
:
: two hubs = two separate buses, a frame on busA never shows up on busB.
: so the experiment gets every OBC message twice, once per bus, and has to
: drop the second copy (experiment/main.c)
:
: to fake a broken bus A at any time (the experiment keeps getting data on B):
:   mach set "obc"
:   connector Disconnect sysbus.can1 busA

$art?=@renode/art/redundant.py
include @renode/two_boards.resc

# second bus --> plug the can2 of each machine into it
emulation CreateCANHub "busB"
mach set "obc"
connector Connect sysbus.can2 busB
mach set "experiment"
connector Connect sysbus.can2 busB
mach clear
